a MUSD loan against their Bitcoin.

4
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:07,600
By October, one was left.

5
00:00:07,850 --> 00:00:09,180
They didn't repay.

6
00:00:09,430 --> 00:00:10,780
They were redeemed.

7
00:00:11,650 --> 00:00:12,440
In wave one,

8
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:15,150
Keel gave new borrowers a safe place.

9
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:16,070
This wave,

10
00:00:16,090 --> 00:00:19,290
Keel goes after the loans Mezo already has.

11
00:00:19,540 --> 00:00:21,170
Three things are new.

12
00:00:22,030 --> 00:00:23,350
Here's a wallet with a

13
00:00:23,370 --> 00:00:25,180
real Mezo loan on testnet.

14
00:00:25,430 --> 00:00:27,030
Redemptions can reach it.

15
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:29,430
Keel reads it and offers a move:

16
00:00:29,450 --> 00:00:31,500
the same Bitcoin, the same debt,

17
00:00:31,520 --> 00:00:33,050
and no MUSD needed.

18
00:00:33,890 --> 00:00:35,480
One signature lets Mezo

19
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:37,400
close the loan for Keel.

20
00:00:37,650 --> 00:00:40,000
Keel pays it off with savers' MUSD,

21
00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:42,060
Mezo sends the Bitcoin across,

22
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:44,990
and the same debt opens again in Keel.

23
00:00:45,860 --> 00:00:46,660
Done.

24
00:00:46,910 --> 00:00:48,360
The Mezo loan is gone,

25
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:50,760
and the same debt now lives in Keel,

26
00:00:50,780 --> 00:00:53,100
where redemptions can't reach it.

27
00:00:53,940 --> 00:00:56,480
Here's that move on Mezo's explorer.

28
00:00:56,730 --> 00:00:59,100
One transaction, start to finish.

29
00:01:00,470 --> 00:01:03,150
Second, locked Bitcoin pays its own loan.

30
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:04,830
A veBTC lock keeps

31
00:01:04,850 --> 00:01:06,860
voting for a Mezo pool.

32
00:01:07,110 --> 00:01:09,840
Every Thursday the pool pays its voters.

33
00:01:10,090 --> 00:01:11,810
Keel collects that share,

34
00:01:11,830 --> 00:01:13,430
swaps any Bitcoin into

35
00:01:13,450 --> 00:01:15,070
MUSD on Mezo's own pool,

36
00:01:15,090 --> 00:01:16,690
and the debt drops.

37
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:19,660
This is the first real payment.

38
00:01:19,910 --> 00:01:21,480
The lock's rewards came in,

39
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:23,540
and the loan's debt went down.

40
00:01:23,790 --> 00:01:25,250
Nobody touched it.

41
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:26,780
Third,

42
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:29,840
Keel runs on Mezo mainnet with real money.

43
00:01:30,090 --> 00:01:32,760
A 48 hour timelock owns the vault,

44
00:01:32,780 --> 00:01:35,540
